steps.prompt:
The FAA chart draws one whole cycle, two turns of the crankshaft, as a spiral. Start at the inner dot just before the top of the circle, which is TDC, and go clockwise. Each half turn is one stroke: intake (orange), compression (green), power (red), exhaust (blue).

Read four events, each in degrees from TDC or BDC:
intake opens 50° before TDC;
intake closes 30° after BDC;
exhaust opens 30° before BDC;
exhaust closes 25° after TDC.

Duration is the angles added. The intake valve is open for 50 + 180 + 30 = 260°. The exhaust valve is open for 30 + 180 + 25 = 235°.

Overlap is the blue arc at the top: 50 + 25 = 75°, with both valves open.

This is an example. Real values vary from engine to engine.
